From 65bb9e9ec7acb54383ef4e77f9f294b2b835dcaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 18:52:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cycle: let LH/BBT evidence and cervical mucus actually adjust
 predictions

- Positive LH test moves the ovulation estimate off the calendar (surge + ~24-36h), when the timing is plausible
- Confirmed BBT temperature shift moves ovulation to the day before the shift, when no LH test exists
- Past cycles with a confirmed BBT shift teach a personal luteal-phase length, replacing the fixed 14-day assumption
- Egg-white cervical mucus logged ahead of the calendar window extends the fertile window earlier
- Fertile window always follows whichever ovulation date won (LH > BBT > calendar)
- Provenance marked 'confirmed'/'high confidence' when evidence-adjusted, vs 'baseline'/'predicted' for pure calendar guesses
- Assistant copy updated: LH tests are no longer described as 'kept separate' from the estimate
- 5 new tests covering LH adjustment, implausible-LH rejection, BBT adjustment, personalized luteal length, and mucus extension
---
